            "target_entity_instance": "Eeyou Istchee coastal waters",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Rapid warming of ice-free surface waters led to unseasonably high sea surface temperatures (SSTs) throughout June-October 1998 (Figure 4C). In total, five high-SST events lasting a total of 79 days occurred during that period that meet the definition of a marine heat wave (MHW; SST exceeding 90th percentile of the baseline for five consecutive days or more (Figure 4D))53. Prior to the 1998 MHWs, there were only two MHWs in Eeyou Istchee coastal waters for the entire 1982-1997 period.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
